## 6. What about `selfCancel`?

Earlier I mentioned patient self-cancel had a penalty. Confirm that `appointmentController.selfCancel` and `appointmentService.selfCancel` no longer call `walletService.cancellationPenalty`. Under the no-penalty rule, `selfCancel` becomes just:

```js
async selfCancel({ actor, appointmentId }) {
  const appointment = await Appointment.findById(appointmentId)
    .populate('patientProfile', 'accountId')
    .populate('session', 'startTime');
  if (!appointment) throw NotFound('Appointment not found');
  if (String(appointment.patientProfile?.accountId) !== String(actor.account._id)) {
    throw Forbidden('Appointment does not belong to this user');
  }
  if (TERMINAL_STATUSES.includes(appointment.status)) {
    throw Conflict(`Cannot cancel an appointment in status "${appointment.status}"`);
  }

  appointment.status      = 'cancelled';
  appointment.cancelledAt = new Date();
  await appointment.save();

  // If the patient already paid via Paymob, mark payment for admin-triggered refund.
  // (Refund itself is handled out-of-band for MVP.)
  return { appointment };
}
```

Also drop these unused constants from `appointmentService.js`:

